<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Turing returns two weeks after his first visit, five weeks after the last estrogen injection. He saw Dr. Montrose-Adeyemi of endocrinology this morning and had a scrotal ultrasound, which was normal. His breasts are still tender against his shirt, with no change in size, and he has had no nipple discharge. Libido and morning erections are still absent. He has had two sessions with the clinic psychologist and found them easier than he expected; they have begun with what was done to him rather than with his sexuality, which he says he has never regarded as the problem. He sleeps five to six hours and has run twice this week, alone. He has had no suicidal thoughts and keeps his safety plan on his phone. He takes cholecalciferol daily. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Breasts</td><td>Still tender; no change in size; no discharge</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual function</td><td>Libido and morning erections still absent</td></tr><tr><td>Psychotherapy</td><td>Two sessions with the clinic psychologist</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep and activity</td><td>Five to six hours; ran twice this week</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No suicidal thoughts since intake; safety plan on his phone</td></tr><tr><td>PHQ-9</td><td>14, down from 15</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

